# The list of things ritz-get knows about. Friends get changes with their next `ritz-get update`.
#
# A line starting with [Name] opens a section; the sections are shown in this order.
# Entries before the first section belong to [Software]. '#' starts a comment only as the
# first non-blank character of a line (so URLs may contain '#').
#
# A program (a git repo with an executable ./install.sh, see SPEC.md):
#   NAME OWNER/REPO [BRANCH] "DESCRIPTION"
# A website (opened with xdg-open, can get a start-menu shortcut):
#   NAME URL "DESCRIPTION"
#
#   NAME         [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*; folder name, command name, icons/NAME.png
#   BRANCH       optional; default is the remote's default branch
#   DESCRIPTION  at most 80 characters, no double quote
#
# Optional indented lines directly under an entry:
#   title: Display Name          at most 40 characters, shown instead of NAME
#   setup: one manual step       at most 120 characters, shown after install; a URL becomes a link
#
# Private repos stay out: other people can not clone them.

[Software]
yt-dlp-gui Ritze03/yt-dlp-gui "Lean Go + Gio desktop GUI for yt-dlp"
  title: yt-dlp GUI
ritz Ritze03/ritz "Linux Steam launch wrapper"
  title: Ritz
ForzaTelemetryV3Launcher Ritze03/ForzaTelemetryV3Launcher "Launcher for Forza Telemetry V3: keeps it up to date, builds and runs it"
  title: Forza Telemetry V3 Launcher
simple-screensharing Ritze03/simple-screensharing "Friends screensharing: native desktop client (E2E-encrypted, low latency)"
  title: Simple Screensharing
  setup: Needs PipeWire (incl. pw-loopback) and GStreamer plugins pipewire/good/bad/libav at runtime
  setup: Needs a relay: self-host from this repo, or use a friend's; the app takes a join link
geofinder Ritze03/geofinder "Geobingo-style multiplayer party game with real Google and Apple Maps"
  title: Geofinder
SteamAlt Ritze03/SteamAlt "Copy Steam game saves and settings between accounts on one PC"
  title: Steam Userdata Copier
gamescope-ritz Ritze03/gamescope-ritz "SteamOS session compositing window manager, with added features"
  title: Gamescope Ritz
  setup: Ritz users: copy its Ritz module by hand, see https://github.com/Ritze03/gamescope-ritz#quick-start

